# Prisma rules

Apply this rule only when the repository intentionally uses Prisma and has a Prisma schema or client dependency. If Prisma is not present, leave this rule dormant and do not introduce it implicitly.

- Use one PrismaClient per process via a `globalThis` singleton. Never create one per request.
- Prefer `select` over `include` — `include` loads whole rows and bloats the typed payload.
- Raw SQL only as a tagged template. For example:
  ```ts
  db.$queryRaw`SELECT ... WHERE email = ${email}`
  ```
- Never `$queryRawUnsafe` with a built-up string. That is SQL injection.
- `db push` is prototype-only. Use `migrate dev` locally, `migrate deploy` in CI.
- Batch with `where: { id: { in: ids } }`. Never query inside a `for` loop.

References:
- Prisma Client setup: https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/prisma-client/setup-and-configuration/instantiate-prisma-client
- Prisma raw queries: https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/prisma-client/using-raw-sql/raw-queries
- Prisma development and production migrations: https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/prisma-migrate/workflows/development-and-production
- Prisma select fields: https://www.prisma.io/docs/orm/prisma-client/queries/select-fields
